Flush buffered vertices before glPushMatrix()

push_matrix() changed the matrix stack (and could realloc it) without
FLUSH_VERTICES(), unlike pop_matrix() and the other matrix calls, so
immediate-mode primitives still in the vbo_exec buffer were then drawn by
classic swrast/tnl with the pushed matrix. Found by the Warzone 2100 port
(textured quads drawn with a texture-matrix scale vanished once QuesoGLC
pushed the texture matrix); checked by tests/host-harness/mesa/render-matrix.

diff --git a/src/mesa/main/matrix.c b/src/mesa/main/matrix.c
--- a/src/mesa/main/matrix.c
+++ b/src/mesa/main/matrix.c
@@ -293,6 +293,8 @@
 push_matrix(struct gl_context *ctx, struct gl_matrix_stack *stack,
             GLenum matrixMode, const char *func)
 {
+   FLUSH_VERTICES(ctx, 0);
+
    if (stack->Depth + 1 >= stack->MaxDepth) {
       if (ctx->Transform.MatrixMode == GL_TEXTURE) {
          _mesa_error(ctx, GL_STACK_OVERFLOW, "%s(mode=GL_TEXTURE, unit=%d)",
